course: dictionary
lesson: 1675
title: Chop: cutting and hitting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chop is a verb with several meanings. Most often it means to cut something into pieces with a knife or an axe. In the kitchen you chop vegetables on a chopping board, and an adult should help with the sharp knife, keeping your fingers curled away from the blade.
explain: Chop can also mean to cut a whole tree so that it falls. Woodcutters chop wood for a fire. Context tells you which meaning is right: «The woodcutter chopped down the old oak» is about a tree, while «Chop the onion into small pieces» is about food.
explain: Chop can be a noun too: a thick slice of meat with a bone, like a pork chop, or a quick, hard hit, like a karate chop. Read the words around it to know which one fits.
fact: Chop means to cut something into pieces with a knife or an axe.
fact: Chop down means to cut a tree so that it falls.
fact: A chop is a thick slice of meat with a bone, such as a pork chop or lamb chop.
fact: A chop can also be a quick, hard hit, as in a karate chop.
fact: «Chop and change» means keep changing your mind, and «get the chop» means be removed.
exercise: «Chop the carrots into small pieces.» What does chop mean here? | To eat them whole | To wash them in cold water | To peel them with a spoon | *To cut into pieces with a knife
exercise: «The woodcutter chopped down the tree.» What does chopped down mean? | To paint the bark | To climb to the top | *To cut a tree so that it falls | To plant a new tree
exercise: «She ordered a pork chop for dinner.» What is a chop in this sentence? | A small piece of bread | *A thick slice of meat with a bone | A quick hit with the hand | A kind of cooking pot
test: «The web page was chopped into small packets.» What does chopped mean here? | Read out loud | *Cut into pieces | Made longer | Painted in bright colours
test: Dad says he will chop and change his mind about the holiday. What does chop and change mean? | Chop wood for the fire | Give a karate chop to the table | Cut the holiday short | *Keep changing your mind
exam: Which one is a karate chop? | A tool for sharpening pencils | A slice of lamb cooked on a grill | *A quick, hard hit with the side of the hand | A long walk through the woods
